---
// Evidence argued by artifact, not by totals: the ledger, the scoreboard,
// and the paper trail a task leaves behind. Anyone can claim a number;
// Continuum's claim is that every number has a file behind it.

const ledger = `<span class="text-text-dim"># task.yaml · the execution ledger, one per task</span>
<span class="text-[#89b4fa]">task:</span> auth-token-rotation
<span class="text-[#89b4fa]">mode:</span> DONE        <span class="text-[#89b4fa]">branch:</span> task/auth-token-rotation
<span class="text-[#89b4fa]">sessions:</span>
  - <span class="text-[#89dceb]">mode:</span> EXPLORING     <span class="text-[#89dceb]">turns:</span> 18  <span class="text-[#89dceb]">cost_usd:</span> 0.24
  - <span class="text-[#89dceb]">mode:</span> RESEARCHING   <span class="text-[#89dceb]">turns:</span> 11  <span class="text-[#89dceb]">cost_usd:</span> 0.14
  - <span class="text-[#89dceb]">mode:</span> PLANNING      <span class="text-[#89dceb]">turns:</span> 24  <span class="text-[#89dceb]">cost_usd:</span> 0.58
  - <span class="text-[#89dceb]">mode:</span> IMPLEMENTING  <span class="text-[#89dceb]">turns:</span> 31  <span class="text-[#89dceb]">cost_usd:</span> 0.72
  - <span class="text-[#89dceb]">mode:</span> VALIDATING    <span class="text-[#89dceb]">turns:</span> 12  <span class="text-[#89dceb]">cost_usd:</span> 0.30
<span class="text-text-dim"># a full task, end to end: ~$2. where time and money go,</span>
<span class="text-text-dim"># per mode, is a question with an answer.</span>`;

const scoreboard = `<span class="text-text-dim">$</span> <span class="text-text-primary">regent scoreboard</span> idea-unify-auth
<span class="text-text-dim">remote: origin/main · sha 91e74f7 · read 18:04Z</span>
auth-shared-middleware      <span class="text-[#a6e3a1]">delivered</span>
auth-token-rotation         <span class="text-[#a6e3a1]">delivered</span>
auth-docs-runbook           <span class="text-[#fab387]">delivered-something-else</span>
<span class="text-text-secondary">checked 8 of 9</span> · 1 could not be read
<span class="text-[#d4af37]">(a gap, not a zero)</span>`;

const trail = `tasks/auth-token-rotation/
├── brief.md          <span class="text-text-dim">what was asked, exactly</span>
├── exploration.md    <span class="text-text-dim">the gate that opened RESEARCHING</span>
├── research.md       <span class="text-text-dim">…that opened PLANNING</span>
├── plan.md · todo.md <span class="text-text-dim">…that opened IMPLEMENTING</span>
├── validation.md     <span class="text-text-dim">what "done" was defined to mean</span>
└── sessions/*.jsonl  <span class="text-text-dim">every session: turns, cost, events</span>`;
---

<section id="evidence" class="py-8 md:py-14 px-6 relative overflow-hidden scroll-mt-14">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="absolute top-0 -right-1/5 w-[700px] h-[600px] rounded-full opacity-[0.10]"
         style="background: radial-gradient(circle, #d4af37 0%, transparent 70%);"></div>
    <div class="absolute bottom-0 -left-1/4 w-[600px] h-[500px] rounded-full opacity-[0.08]"
         style="background: radial-gradient(circle, #89b4fa 0%, transparent 70%);"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="continuum-rule max-w-7xl mx-auto absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-full"></div>
  <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    <span class="eyebrow mb-4 block" style="color: #d4af37;">Evidence</span>
    <h2 class="text-[1.875rem] md:text-[2.5rem] max-w-[640px] mb-4">
      The proof is a file you can open.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-text-muted max-w-[640px] mb-12">
      Anyone can put a big number on a landing page. Continuum's claim is stronger and
      easier to check: every task run since 2025 (own products, a real enterprise
      engagement, the studio behind it) left artifacts behind, because the artifacts
      <strong>are the mechanism</strong>. Verify progress with nothing more exotic than
      reading a directory.
    </p>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
      <!-- The ledger -->
      <div class="glass-card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#89b4fa]"></span>
          <h3 class="text-[0.9375rem]">The ledger: cost is recorded, not estimated</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block"><pre><code set:html={ledger} /></pre></div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.78125rem] text-text-muted">
          Which mode is expensive, whether a task was badly sized, where the week
          actually went: answered from the ledger, not from memory. A supervisor can be
          wrong about their own system and find out.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- The scoreboard -->
      <div class="glass-card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#d4af37]"></span>
          <h3 class="text-[0.9375rem]">The scoreboard: done is read off the remote</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block"><pre><code set:html={scoreboard} /></pre></div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.78125rem] text-text-muted">
          Delivery verdicts are computed against the remote ref, never the local
          checkout, headed by the sha and when it was read. A task that publishes
          "done" against the evidence gets flagged, and an unreadable check reports
          as a gap instead of quietly passing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-10">
      <!-- The paper trail -->
      <div class="glass-card p-6">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#a6e3a1]"></span>
          <h3 class="text-[0.9375rem]">The record: a byproduct, not a chore</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block"><pre><code set:html={trail} /></pre></div>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[0.78125rem] text-text-muted">
          By the time a task finishes it holds a written account of its own reasoning.
          None of it was produced as documentation; each file existed because it was
          the gate that let the next mode begin.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- The reference run -->
      <div class="glass-card p-6 flex flex-col">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#cba6f7]"></span>
          <h3 class="text-[0.9375rem]">One run, end to end</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[0.8125rem] text-text-muted">
          One captured signal, a few lines long, went in. Out came 17 findings, 9
          decisions, 22 executable briefs and 22 GitHub issues; the refinery did the
          expanding. A typical run completes without the human touching it at all:
          regent arbitrates the routine with a recorded rationale, and escalates only
          a scope call, a fact only you know, or an outward-facing effect.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-text-dim leading-loose">
          <span>signal</span>
          <span class="text-surface1"> ── </span><span class="text-[#89dceb]">17 findings</span>
          <span class="text-surface1"> ── </span><span class="text-[#89b4fa]">9 decisions</span>
          <span class="text-surface1"> ── </span><span class="text-[#cba6f7]">22 briefs</span>
          <span class="text-surface1"> ── </span><span class="text-[#a6e3a1]">22 issues</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-auto pt-4 text-[0.8125rem] italic text-text-secondary border-l-2 border-[rgba(212,175,55,0.5)] pl-4">
          "This abstraction let me abstract from every detail and participate only where
          I was actually needed."
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The totals, demoted to a footnote strip -->
    <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 font-mono text-[0.6875rem] text-text-dim">
      <span>in production since 2025</span>
      <span>1,000+ tasks across multiple real organizations</span>
      <span>3,057 recorded sessions · 45,485 turns</span>
      <span>every figure from the system's own ledger</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
